	(text "Relay 3 (battery stopper): drive PB3, INA226 U4 at 0x44"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "ee64fc62-5236-5865-b5d0-dab74837e2d2")
	)
	(text "No coil feedback: PA0-PA3 drive the winch and the servo UART; the INA226 does the diagnosis.\nINA226 0x44 (A1 = VS, A0 = GND): load current (30 mΩ, LSB 100 µA) + 24 V rail; ALERT → PA15.\nLED6: output ON; its 6.7 mA also lets the INA226 see the contact close with no load.\nF5: 3A hold PTC, so a shorted output trips only this channel. D16: load flyback.\nQ4 AO3400A: R17 100 Ω gate, R18 100k pull-down = OFF in reset (CIF §7a)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 91.44 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "83363ec9-1b98-5a33-8e04-ab312f801743")
	)
	(text "Relay 4 (spare): drive PA7, INA226 U5 at 0x45"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 127 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "7081a525-9ba7-5991-b6fc-2be68a2bef76")
	)
	(text "No coil feedback: PA0-PA3 drive the winch and the servo UART; the INA226 does the diagnosis.\nINA226 0x45 (A1 = VS, A0 = VS): load current (30 mΩ, LSB 100 µA) + 24 V rail; ALERT → PA15.\nLED7: output ON; its 6.7 mA also lets the INA226 see the contact close with no load.\nF6: 3A hold PTC, so a shorted output trips only this channel. D17: load flyback.\nQ5 AO3400A: R20 100 Ω gate, R21 100k pull-down = OFF in reset (CIF §7a)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 269.24 195.58 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "4a09c11b-bfe4-5e30-9720-a38ba7de09f5")
	)
	(text "Loads (CIF §7, all 24 V DC)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "5f9c8a9c-9246-5060-bd63-2bc8c9b15cb4")
	)
	(text "CH1 safety light: Hanyoung T084-PAD24Y-D\n   (LED + motor). Current TBD: measure,\n   then set its window (est. 0.1-0.3 A).\nCH2 LED DRL: ≤ 2 A continuous.\nCH3 battery stopper: Heschen HS-1564B 24 V\n   push-pull solenoid, 1.5 A, intermittent\n   (80 °C after 3 min continuous): firmware\n   enforces a maximum on-time + cool-down.\nCH4 spare: ≤ 2 A continuous.\n\nEvery channel: 24 V / 2 A continuous,\n3A hold PTC per output (CIF §7a: fuse\nper channel). Shunt on the supply side of the\ncontact, so the INA226 never sees the load\nflyback (−0.7 V < −0.3 V input limit) and a\nwelded contact still shows current while OFF.\n\nInductive loads (solenoid): SS34 flyback at\neach output on the board; also fit an SS14-class\ndiode at the solenoid itself.\n\nCoil budget: 4 × 71 mA ≈ 285 mA from +5V_24\n(U1 URB2405S, 1.2 A).\nAll relays OFF in reset / boot / firmware\nupdate: 100k gate pull-downs; PA8 reads LOW in\nreset (UCPD pull-down), PA7 is pulled DOWN by\nthe bootloader (CIF §2c)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 27.94 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "35df0560-61b6-597e-b7ee-c1c4d75950e6")
	)
